      "writtenOn": "2023-08-11T19:51:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like the return type should now be `union dp_cable_type_flags`, and the bit operations below should just be assignments to the fields. The usage up in `svdm_dp_config` wouldn\u0027t need to assign directly to `raw_value`, so this type can probably just a struct and not a union. It seems like you should also be able to delete the flag macros and just use true/false.\n\nThis part is a nit: `dp_cable_type_flags` could be simpler as\n```\nstruct dp_cable_type_flags {\n    bool optical;\n    bool active;\n    bool retimer;\n};\n```\nIt would still fit in a register and this code isn\u0027t very performance sensitive anyway, so it doesn\u0027t seem to me like there\u0027s much value in using bit fields to make it smaller than the 3 bytes it would naively occupy.",
      "revId": "919b3fb238584d44b8aa3ea0a1e05ee79175e3aa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
