      "writtenOn": "2023-08-11T19:51:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks like another instance where my suggestion turned out to be harder than I expected. 😞\n1. This function seems like it\u0027s intended to return a value that could be placed into the SVDM version major and minor fields of a VDM. So something like `0101b` for version 2.1. What it\u0027s returning currently is `01b /* major */ | 01b \u003c\u003c 11 /* minor */`.\n2. The existing usages of this function expect the result to be unshifted, so they pass it into `VDO_SVDM_VERS_MAJOR`, which shifts it by 13 bits. So the bits that get written to the VDO are `01b \u003c\u003c 13 /* correct place for major */ | 01b \u003c\u003c (11 + 13) /* middle of SVID field */`. It just so happens that the 1 errantly in the middle of the SVID is already set in the case of the PD SID (0xff00) or DP VID (0xff01). It would turn the TBT VID from 0x8087 to 0x9087. Existing usages also compare the return value directly to, e.g. `SVDM_VER_2_0`.\n3. Because this call chain does not actually set the minor version, the existing call sites still need to OR in `VDM_VERS_MINOR` as they did before this function was changed.\n\nAs it is, this is wrong. While I don\u0027t like the idea of introducing the minor version as a separate object, I think the refactor to make this function return both of them in a usable way would be non-trivial and out of scope for this change. Sorry for leading you down this rabbit hole.\n\nSo I\u0027d suggest removing `VDM_VERS_MINOR` from `pd_get_vdo_ver`. I think most of the existing usages already add in `VDM_VERS_MINOR` at the callsite, but you should double check that all of them do.",
      "revId": "919b3fb238584d44b8aa3ea0a1e05ee79175e3aa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a9499986_09a5ca76",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
