      "writtenOn": "2023-08-11T19:51:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I gave you incorrect instructions before. `VDO_CMDT_MASK` is for the Command Type field at bits 6-7. This field in most cases should be 0 for REQ. ORing `VDO_CMDT_MASK` in here would set it to BUSY, which would generally be wrong.\n\nI don\u0027t think we have a named mask/constructor for the Command field, and you don\u0027t need to add one if you don\u0027t want to. If we did have one, it would be something like,\n```\n#define VDO_CMD_MASK 0x1f\n...\n#define VDO_CMD(cmd) (cmd \u0026 0x1f)\n```\n\nLong-term, this function should be generalized to produce SVDM command types other than REQ. In the short term, if you named it `pd_compose_svdm_req_header`, it would be correct in its existing usages.",
      "revId": "919b3fb238584d44b8aa3ea0a1e05ee79175e3aa",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
